    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "four heavy-row exceptional roots sharpen factor degrees and exclude two d_A=1 profiles",
    "statement": "For each irreducible split-biform factor, its classified grid uses Rm_j supported-fiber points and the heavy row can use only the remaining slack sigma_j=3en_j-Rm_j. Since g_* supplies e-6 supported heavy-row roots, the total factorwise root deficit is at most four. Hence large odd factors satisfy (q-2)m_j>=3e-8 and huge even factors satisfy (q-2)m_j>=6e-8. At d_A=1 this excludes the two-large-odd and huge-even trichotomy profiles, leaving one large odd factor and ordinary-even companions.",
